{"name":"Turbulent Sea","hex":"#536a79","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turbulent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Violently disturbed or agitated; tempestuous, tumultuous.","Being in, or causing, disturbance or unrest."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turbulent"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Turbulence","blocks":[{"text":"In fluid dynamics, turbulence or turbulent flow is fluid motion exhibiting chaotic changes in pressure and flow velocity. It is in contrast to laminar flow, which occurs when a fluid flows in parallel layers with no disruption between those layers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turbulence"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg/500px-Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg/500px-Los_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Laminar and turbulent water flow over the hull of a submarine. As the relative velocity of the water increases, turbulence occurs.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALos_Angeles_attack_sub_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/1280px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg/500px-Airplane_vortex_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Turbulence in the tip vortex from an airplane wing passing through coloured smoke ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAirplane_vortex_edit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg/330px-False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg/330px-False_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flow visualization of a turbulent jet, made by laser-induced fluorescence. The jet exhibits a wide range of length scales, an important characteristic of turbulent flows.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFalse_color_image_of_the_far_field_of_a_submerged_turbulent_jet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg/500px-Laminar-turbulent_transition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=